  "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Transportation_Problem\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 300)  # Set time limit to 300 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    sources = list(range(10))  # S0..S9\n    destinations = list(range(7))  # D0..D6\n\n    supplies = [82, 98, 43, 70, 49, 50, 66, 21, 91, 31]\n    demands = [60, 43, 39, 16, 40, 45, 74]\n\n    # Cost matrix: rows correspond to sources S0..S9, columns to destinations D0..D6\n    costs = [\n        [ 27.23,  16.87,  22.37,   6.00,  24.35,  14.18,   9.85],  # S0\n        [ 17.61,   9.92,  17.37,   5.34,  18.17,  10.58,  15.64],  # S1\n        [  5.79,   6.12,  18.77,   5.43,  21.43,  11.89,  18.58],  # S2\n        [  6.59,  17.15,   9.31,  19.34,  16.96,  29.34,   8.43],  # S3\n        [  5.78,  15.88,  13.15,  23.95,  16.69,  12.61,  25.08],  # S4\n        [ 26.27,  16.08,  29.66,  20.43,  27.47,  20.71,  17.29],  # S5\n        [ 12.40,  21.18,  13.53,  25.49,  17.48,  16.26,  26.80],  # S6\n        [ 27.97,   8.33,  23.80,  11.83,  14.59,  23.21,   6.84],  # S7\n        [ 26.20,  17.59,  11.93,  25.65,  27.16,  13.93,  14.97],  # S8\n        [ 19.36,   8.59,   9.17,  22.30,  25.65,  13.38,   7.38],  # S9\n    ]\n\n    # Decision variables:\n    # Flow_S{i}_D{j} >= 0 is the quantity shipped from source i to destination j\n    flows = {}\n    for i in sources:\n        for j in destinations:\n            flows[(i, j)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_S{i}_D{j}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total transportation cost\n    m.setObjective(\n        quicksum(costs[i][j] * flows[(i, j)] for i in sources for j in destinations),\n        GRB.MINIMIZE\n    )\n\n    # Supply constraints: Shipments from each source <= its supply\n    for i in sources:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for j in destinations) <= supplies[i],\n            name=f\"Supply_S{i}\"\n        )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Shipments to each destination >= its demand\n    for j in destinations:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for i in sources) >= demands[j],\n            name=f\"Demand_D{j}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
  "LLM_description": "Subject: Multi-source distribution plan to meet demand at lowest cost\nDate: March 19, 2026\n\nSituation:\n- We operate a network of multiple source locations supplying several destination locations.\n- Freight spend is a major driver of unit economics, and improved routing and allocation will enhance margins without compromising service.\n- Customer satisfaction depends on timely deliveries and complete orders; stockouts and late shipments lead to lost sales and escalations.\n- Partial shipments are allowed; orders can be split across sources and routes, and quantities do not need to be in whole pallet or truckload increments.\n\nProblem:\n- Determine how much to ship from each source to each destination so that no source exceeds its available inventory and every destination receives its required quantity.\n- Route-specific shipping costs vary; the plan should favor lower-cost lanes while still meeting all service requirements.\n- The outcome should be a clear, executable shipping plan that minimizes total transportation cost, aligns with inventory realities, and supports on-time delivery.\n- Once the recommended allocations are confirmed, transportation will tender loads against the selected lanes and planning will monitor adherence and exceptions.\n\nAnnex \u2013 Shipping Data:\nDestination requirements: Store D1 needs 43 units; Store D6 needs 74 units; Store D4 needs 40 units; Store D5 needs 45 units; Store D3 needs 16 units; Store D0 needs 60 units; Store D2 needs 39 units.\n\nShipping costs by source:\n  Warehouse S0 (supply: 82 units): D6 at $9.85/unit, D5 at $14.18/unit, D0 at $27.23/unit, D3 at $6.00/unit, D1 at $16.87/unit, D2 at $22.37/unit, D4 at $24.35/unit\n  Warehouse S1 (supply: 98 units): D2 at $17.37/unit, D1 at $9.92/unit, D4 at $18.17/unit, D6 at $15.64/unit, D5 at $10.58/unit, D3 at $5.34/unit, D0 at $17.61/unit\n  Warehouse S2 (supply: 43 units): D6 at $18.58/unit, D4 at $21.43/unit, D5 at $11.89/unit, D0 at $5.79/unit, D3 at $5.43/unit, D2 at $18.77/unit, D1 at $6.12/unit\n  Warehouse S3 (supply: 70 units): D2 at $9.31/unit, D4 at $16.96/unit, D3 at $19.34/unit, D0 at $6.59/unit, D5 at $29.34/unit, D1 at $17.15/unit, D6 at $8.43/unit\n  Warehouse S4 (supply: 49 units): D2 at $13.15/unit, D0 at $5.78/unit, D3 at $23.95/unit, D5 at $12.61/unit, D6 at $25.08/unit, D1 at $15.88/unit, D4 at $16.69/unit\n  Warehouse S5 (supply: 50 units): D4 at $27.47/unit, D3 at $20.43/unit, D2 at $29.66/unit, D1 at $16.08/unit, D0 at $26.27/unit, D5 at $20.71/unit, D6 at $17.29/unit\n  Warehouse S6 (supply: 66 units): D1 at $21.18/unit, D4 at $17.48/unit, D6 at $26.80/unit, D5 at $16.26/unit, D3 at $25.49/unit, D0 at $12.40/unit, D2 at $13.53/unit\n  Warehouse S7 (supply: 21 units): D1 at $8.33/unit, D0 at $27.97/unit, D6 at $6.84/unit, D5 at $23.21/unit, D3 at $11.83/unit, D2 at $23.80/unit, D4 at $14.59/unit\n  Warehouse S8 (supply: 91 units): D6 at $14.97/unit, D0 at $26.20/unit, D1 at $17.59/unit, D4 at $27.16/unit, D3 at $25.65/unit, D5 at $13.93/unit, D2 at $11.93/unit\n  Warehouse S9 (supply: 31 units): D3 at $22.30/unit, D6 at $7.38/unit, D5 at $13.38/unit, D1 at $8.59/unit, D4 at $25.65/unit, D0 at $19.36/unit, D2 at $9.17/unit",
